    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Who should choose AccuWeb?</h2><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">AccuWeb fits buyers who want <strong>enterprise-grade infrastructure at a mid-budget rate</strong> — dedicated vCPUs with no overselling, ECC RAM, RAID-10 pure SSD, and SOC 2 Type II certified data centers across a genuinely global 16+ DC footprint. The managed option (setup, guidance, under-15-minute critical support) makes it a strong fit for small businesses and non-sysadmin owners who want a production host without managing the whole stack. The 16+ locations spanning the US, Canada, Europe, APAC, India, and South Africa give it broader geographic reach than most budget hosts.</p><p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-8">It is not the right fit if you need the absolute lowest entry sticker price (RackNerd at $1.99/mo wins), 30+ regions with per-hour billing (Vultr), or high-capacity always-on DDoS scrubbing. The promos are aggressive ($4.95/mo Edge) but renew at a higher standard list, and the entry plan is single-vCPU. AccuWeb's angle is managed, enterprise-grade infrastructure — a genuine differentiator from the budget unmanaged KVM that dominates this price band.</p>
